  "answer": "I found **two RFPs with explicit Iran-related respondent requirements**:\n\n| RFP | Requirement |\n|---|---|\n| **NYC Board of Education Retirement System, Investment Consulting Services (RFP #2024-003)** | Proposers must submit a signed, verified **Iran Divestment Act certification** that they are not on New York State’s list of entities engaged in investment activities in Iran’s energy sector. A proposer unable to certify must submit a signed, detailed explanation; without the required certification, its proposal will not be considered for award. See Attachment G and the bidder certification, pp. 54–55. |\n| **Illinois State Retirement Systems, Actuarial Consulting Services (Reference #24100)** | A vendor **not using an Illinois Procurement Gateway registration number** must complete and return the “Disclosure of Business Operations with Iran” form as part of its responsive proposal. See §IV.L, p. 13. |\n\n**Important exclusion:** The Los Angeles Fire and Police Pensions financial-statement audit RFP reproduces an Iran Contracting Act affidavit provision in its standard-contract appendix, but its own general terms **expressly exempt this procurement from that provision**. It should not be counted as imposing an Iran affidavit requirement on these respondents. See pp. 25 and 42 of *RFP DCFS25-01*.",
